  "statement": "Solve $\\ln x+\\ln([$a])=\\ln(2)$ for $x>0$.\n\n[__________]{a}",
  "hints": [
    "Use the product rule for logs.",
    "Match the positive arguments.",
    "Divide by the multiplier on $x$."
  ],
  "solution": "The equation is $\\ln([$a]x)=\\ln2$. Thus $[$a]x=2$ and $x=2/[$a]$.",
